## Best Practices

### 1. Always Validate Input

```typescript
// Every endpoint should validate
const validation = validateQueryParams(url, [...]);
if (!validation.valid) {
  return validationErrorResponse(validation.errors, requestId);
}
```

### 2. Always Handle Errors

```typescript
// Use try-catch or asyncHandler
try {
  // Your code
} catch (error) {
  return createErrorResponse(error, requestId, path);
}
```

### 3. Always Include CORS

```typescript
// All responses need CORS headers
headers: {
  'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  'Access-Control-Allow-Origin': '*'
}
```

### 4. Always Track Requests

```typescript
// Generate requestId at start
const requestId = Date.now().toString(36);

// Use in logs
console.log(`[${requestId}] ...`);

// Include in response
return new Response(JSON.stringify({ ...data, requestId }));
```

### 5. Always Log Appropriately

```typescript
// Start of request
console.log(`[${requestId}] 📥 Incoming request: ${method} ${path}`);

// Success
console.log(`[${requestId}] ✅ Found ${count} records`);

// Error
console.error(`[${requestId}] ❌ Error:`, error);
```

